WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 06 · Course 3 · Prove & Show · For entrepreneurs
MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Build evidence into your idea from the start: track, test and share whether it makes a difference, and decide.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:31.356
This module helps you build evidence into your idea from the start: how you will track progress, test whether it makes a difference, listen to the people you serve and learn. It answers: how will we know it works, and for whom?

4
00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:32.356
Why evidence from day one

5
00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:37.659
1. Without a baseline captured now, you cannot show change later.

6
00:00:37.659 --> 00:00:43.704
2. Early evidence tells you what works before you spend money growing it.

7
00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:51.119
3. Listening to the people you serve respects their dignity and improves the work.

8
00:00:51.519 --> 00:01:02.119
What you will work through: 6.1 MEAL principles and a proportionate system · 6.2 From Theory of Change to results framework · 6.3 Indicators · 6.4 Baselines and targets · 6.5 Data collection, ethics and data quality · 6.6 The MEAL plan and budget · 6.7 Monitoring: planned versus actual · 6.8 Evaluation · 6.9 Accountability: participation, feedback and complaints · 6.10 Learning and adaptive management · 6.11 Reporting and communicating evidence · 6.12 Recap: MEAL

9
00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:03.119
What you will have

10
00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:08.422
1. A results framework with clear indicators, baselines and realistic targets.

11
00:01:08.422 --> 00:01:15.207
2. An ethical data plan and simple ways for people to give feedback or complain.

12
00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:21.141
3. A learning routine and reports suited to each audience.

13
00:01:21.541 --> 00:01:22.141
Keep it usable

14
00:01:22.141 --> 00:01:29.296
1. Size it to what you can keep up; a few indicators beat many abandoned ones.

15
00:01:29.296 --> 00:01:35.711
2. Use your Theory of Change pathways as the starting point for every indicator.

16
00:01:35.711 --> 00:01:43.126
3. Our example bakery tracks trainees who finish, jobs found and weekly food waste.

17
00:01:43.726 --> 00:01:45.726
You create: Your MEAL framework: indicators, baselines, data plan, feedback channels, learning routine and reporting.

18
00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:50.526
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:52.026 --> 00:01:55.126
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
